@prefix rk:   <https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .

<https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk/gating-violation>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://sool.davidkoepsell.com/ontology/rk> ;
    rdfs:label "Gating rule violation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment """This file MUST make the ontology inconsistent.

Stratum D presupposes acts. Here a pragmatic contradiction is asserted to be
part of an artifact that has no act specification, which is the one thing the
gating rule forbids. If a reasoner reports this consistent, the gating rule is
documented but not enforced.

Typing the artifact as rk:ActEmptyArtifact is a closure assertion and is
deliberate: OWL will not conclude the absence of a part on its own, so the
absence has to be stated. That is the honest form of the claim, and it is not
the same as minting an individual to carry a status of 'absent'.

This is a different failure from mask-violation.ttl and must be tested
separately."""@en .

rk:chainlessArtifact a owl:NamedIndividual , rk:ActEmptyArtifact ;
    rdfs:label "an artifact that performs no recognition act"@en .

rk:pragmaticFailure_1 a owl:NamedIndividual , rk:KD3 ;
    rdfs:label "a pragmatic contradiction asserted in an act-empty artifact"@en ;
    obo:BFO_0000050 rk:chainlessArtifact .
